      "pronunciationText": "Last video, our ratio points traced this curve, y equals the natural log of x. It answers questions that start with how long. A new app has a thousand users, and each user brings in one new user a week. So after x weeks, it has e to the x thousand users. Turn that around, and the time to reach x thousand users is the natural log of x weeks. Here's a tempting guess. E to the x is its own derivative, and the natural log undoes e to the x. So is the natural log its own derivative too? Look at x equals a half. The curve is below the axis there, so the natural log of a half is negative. But the curve is still climbing. A climbing curve has a positive gradient, so the guess fails. Then what is the gradient of this curve, and why?"
    },
