      "pronunciationText": "Here's the whole reason. On e to the x, the slope at each point equals its height. The reflection turns that height into the x coordinate on the natural log curve. And it turns the slope into one over itself. So on the natural log curve, the slope at x is one over x. At height four, e to the x has slope four. After the reflection, x is four, and the slope is a quarter. At height a half, the slope a half becomes two, at x equals a half. That's why gradient times x is always one. The app says the same thing. With four thousand users, new users arrive at four thousand a week, so the next thousand takes about a quarter of a week."
    },
